# Implementation

The program implements the following methods:

| Method | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `__init__()` | Initializes the array with a capacity of 1. |
| `__len__()` | Returns the current number of stored elements. |
| `__getitem__()` | Retrieves an element using its index. |
| `append()` | Adds a new element to the array and resizes when necessary. |
| `_resize()` | Doubles the capacity and copies all existing elements. |
| `_make_array()` | Allocates a new ctypes array with the specified capacity. |

---

# Algorithm

1. Create an empty dynamic array.
2. Set the initial capacity to **1**.
3. Insert elements one at a time.
4. Before every insertion:
   - Check whether the array is already full.
   - If full, allocate a new array with **double the current capacity**.
   - Copy all existing elements into the new array.
5. Store the new element.
6. Increase the size counter.
7. Repeat until all elements are inserted.

